    "body": "Might be worth exploring the installation of BBS nodes using micro controllers like nRF52 etc... to temporarily store messages and sync with anyone walking past. <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulletin_board_system>\n\nEven better if you allow for messages to hop between BBS nodes.\n\nYou might need these nodes to have an SD card so that you have enough space to do a store and forward capability.\n\nThis would allow for more persistent communications with threads by allowing passerby to do an active sync of particular messages from a thread (but at a cost to anonymity as the BBS node if compromised will be able to tell that someone near the area is trying to access specific kind of messages)\n\n",
